WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.720
This video covers getting
audio into noctune on the

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.510
web, and what to do when
something interrupts it.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.910
Choose New Encounter, pick your
patient, and select Record from web.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.550
Use Pause and Resume as needed, then Stop.

00:00:12.995 --> 00:00:16.825
The take joins the queue, and Process
1 file sends it for processing.

00:00:17.673 --> 00:00:19.663
Have audio from another device?

00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:23.823
Drop the file into the recording
area, or choose browse files.

00:00:24.073 --> 00:00:28.463
Most common audio formats work,
up to 500 megabytes per file.

00:00:28.793 --> 00:00:30.543
Then choose Process 1 file.

00:00:31.173 --> 00:00:34.133
If the connection drops during
an upload, the take stays in

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.323
the queue, and noctune tells
you the upload didn't finish.

00:00:37.653 --> 00:00:40.203
Choose Process 1 file again to retry.

00:00:40.453 --> 00:00:42.283
Nothing needs to be recorded twice.

00:00:43.007 --> 00:00:46.997
While you record, noctune keeps
a recovery copy in this browser.

00:00:47.087 --> 00:00:51.237
If the tab closes or reloads
mid-recording, open noctune again.

00:00:51.407 --> 00:00:55.717
Recover recordings lists the take, so
you can upload, download, or discard it.

00:00:55.982 --> 00:00:59.492
If that upload fails
too, choose Retry upload.

00:00:59.902 --> 00:01:02.702
Files you add with browse
files aren't kept this way,

00:01:02.702 --> 00:01:05.012
so leave the tab open until
they finish uploading.
